  "map_info": {
    "name": "Voxel Noise: Discretizing the Continuum",
    "title": "Noise Carved into Blocks",
    "lookup_name": "Noise_Voxel",
    "description": "A fixed Perlin field becomes a sampled occupancy decision. A cased 24-cubed model controls a twenty-five-times-larger volume of one-metre cells inside a 28-metre glass flight enclosure with matching cells. A live screen compares one horizontal score slice with the exact occupied/empty mask; the dark orb keeps its independent pulse. Threshold changes classification, CELL selects a sample and screen layer, marked at the corresponding height and address in the large volume, SEED changes the field, and CUT changes only the model view. Connected occupied cells do not establish a walkable route.",
